  "final_message": "I fixed the bug. A subscription now goes back to `active` once its retried payment succeeds, and the full suite passes (24 tests).\n\nThe bug was in `recover` in `billing/dunning.py`. When the retried invoice was paid and no other invoices were still open, the code ran `pass` where it should have moved the subscription to `active`. So the subscription stayed `past_due`. I replaced the `pass` with `transition(ctx, subscription, \"active\")`.\n\nI didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so the 24 passing tests don't include it. `answer.json` in the repo root contains `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"recover\"}`.",
